          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "8.3",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "ebf1ba63c404f36a89caddaa6fe5f69242fcb30f0ba18d9b0a595b1226f560fa",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0001",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 8.3,
              "timestamp": "2026-11-20 13:43:30 UTC",
              "target": "/workspace/agentcore-superagent-update (super-agent/backend)",
              "endpoint": "/api/knowledge-bases/*",
              "method": "GET/PUT/DELETE/POST",
              "cwe": "CWE-639",
              "impact": "Cross-tenant breach of knowledge-base confidentiality and integrity: an authenticated member of organization A can enumerate knowledge-base IDs and read org B's knowledge bases (names, descriptions, file listings), rename/soft-delete them, and modify or delete org B's uploaded knowledge files. Knowledge bases aggregate a tenant's RAG document corpus, so this exposes another tenant's content metadata and allows destructive modification.",
              "technical_analysis": "Route `src/routes/knowledge-base.routes.ts` guards every endpoint only with `[authenticate, requireModifyAccess]` — a role check, not a tenant check. Handlers call `knowledgeBaseService.findById(request.params.id)` etc. without passing `request.user.orgId`. In `src/services/knowledge-base.service.ts`:\n- `findById` (line 69): `prisma.knowledge_bases.findUnique({ where: { id } })` — no `organization_id` filter.\n- `update` (line 80) and `delete` (line 91): `update({ where: { id } })` — mutates any org's KB.\n- `renameFolder` (200), `deleteFolder` (215), `listFolders` (190): unscoped by organization.\n- File handlers in the route operate on `knowledge_files` by bare id.\n\nContrast with the correctly-scoped pattern in `credential-vault.repository.ts:37` (`findFirst({ where: { id, organization_id } })`), which shows the missing control.",
              "remediation_steps": "Add organization scoping at the service layer: `findById(id, organizationId)` must use `findFirst({ where: { id, organization_id } })` (the pattern already used by `credential-vault.repository.ts`), and `update`/`delete`/folder/file operations must verify the parent record's organization before mutating. Alternatively, enforce org checks in the routes and pass `request.user.orgId` into every service call.",
              "counterevidence": "Checked for mitigations: no `requireScopeAccess`/`requireAgentAccess` on these routes, no org filter in `knowledge-base.service.ts` read/update/delete/findById calls, and no global authz hook in route registration (`src/routes/index.ts` registers `knowledgeBaseRoutes` with a bare prefix). Only `listByOrganization` and `create` scope by org. No WAF or gateway-layer tenant filter exists in this codebase. The local repro follows production Prisma `where`-clause semantics exactly.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "If knowledge-base IDs were unguessable and never leaked this would not reduce the demonstrated IDOR; only confirmation of an upstream gateway tenant filter (none exists in this codebase) would lower severity.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Authenticate as a member of org A. 2. GET /api/knowledge-bases/:id with an org B knowledge-base ID — 200 with org B data (organization_id of org B returned). 3. PUT /api/knowledge-bases/:id — renames org B's KB. 4. GET /api/knowledge-bases/:id/files — lists org B file records; PUT .../files/:fileId changes display metadata; DELETE .../files/:fileId removes org B's file record. 5. DELETE /api/knowledge-bases/:id soft-deletes org B's KB.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
