        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-22",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Path traversal + git argument injection in plugin installation (installPlugins)\n\nThe scope-plugin installation path (WorkspaceManager.installPlugins) joins an attacker-controlled plugin name into the filesystem without any traversal check, and passes an attacker-controlled git URL into git clone as a positional argument. An authenticated user with modify access on a business scope can make the backend git-clone a repository into an arbitrary directory outside the session workspace (arbitrary file write), and can inject git options such as --upload-pack to execute an arbitrary command."
