          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Hardcoded bypassPermissions with bypassable regex denylist enables unapproved arbitrary shell execution on backend host via agent tool calls\n\nThe backend's Claude agent runs with a hardcoded `permissionMode: 'bypassPermissions'` and `allowDangerouslySkipPermissions: true`. The only remaining guard is a small regex denylist (`dangerousCommandBlocker`) that is trivially bypassed, so any prompt the agent acts on — including instructions injected via retrieved documents, skills, or web content — results in arbitrary shell command execution on the backend host without any human approval."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
              }
            },
